{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Pethorah.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): it is the name of his place, which is why it says, 'the land of the children of his people,' and they were Arameans, for thus it is written (Deuteronomy 23:5): מפתור ארם נהרים." "<b>And by way of </b>the Midrash: Pethorah is called Pethorah from the root of פתרון (interpretation of dreams), because at first he would interpret dreams, and afterward he became a soothsayer, and afterward he attained to ru'aḥ ha-kodesh."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:34:49.898795274Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}